    "description": "4-Hop-Variance-v3: H=4,K=2 (16 leaves), stationary, deliberately engineered. Two dominant, diametrically-opposed job archetypes (J0 small/small p=0.42 -> always-A path; J1 large/large p=0.42 -> always-B path) plus 5 rare archetypes (p=0.02-0.04) for good Sigma conditioning. Each server is CHEAP in its own regime and EXPENSIVE in the other's (symmetric magnitude), and cross-purpose leakage is zeroed out (decode servers carry no prefill cost and vice versa) so the [1,2] min-max normalization's constant-shift dilution effect is minimized. Targets eps-EXP3/UNIFORM excess cost >20% vs optimal (well above it, by design margin)."
